Tables in the outer margin
==========================

Use widetable for a table that fits on one page. Give tabularx the local
\linewidth and an X column wherever text should wrap. Captions and labels
work like those in a standard table.

    \begin{widetable}[tbp]
      \caption{Evaluation conditions}\label{tab:evaluation-conditions}
      \begin{tabularx}{\linewidth}{@{}l X@{}}
        \toprule
        Condition & Description \\
        \midrule
        In-distribution & Initial pose near the training configuration. \\
        \bottomrule
      \end{tabularx}
    \end{widetable}

For a table that spans pages, place a longtable inside widetablepages.
This starts a fresh page and restores the regular text block after the
final row. Use longtable's \endfirsthead and \endhead to repeat column
headings. Chapters/Appendix.tex contains the full trial table.

